WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.388
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.590
SPEAKER: Welcome to the
Quickstart for Cloud Bigtable.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:12.760
On the Bigtable page,
select Create Instance.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.129
Under Instance Name,
type Quickstart Instance.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:19.660
This should auto-populate
the instance ID for you.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.600
For this Quickstart,
select Development

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.880
as the instance type.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.600
Under Zone, select us-east-1c.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.610
Then click Create.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.950
Once the instance
has been created,

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.080
open Google Cloud Shell.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:42.050
And after it's initialized, type
in gcloud components update,

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:47.340
followed by gcloud
components install cbt.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.850
Then insert the project
and instance information

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.400
into the CBT RC file.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.800
We can now create
our first Bigtable

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.970
by calling cbt
createtable my-table.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:04.860
We can confirm its
creation by typing cbt ls.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.570
We will now create a new family
for the table and call it cf1.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:15.600
We can confirm its creation
by typing cbt ls my-table.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.540
Now we can use the
cbt set command

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:21.570
to set a key value
pair in our table,

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:25.620
and use cbt read to verify
that the key value was

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.270
stored properly.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:30.360
Congratulations, you've
completed the Quickstart.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.710
[MUSIC PLAYING]

